    <instructions>
**Required Fields**
subject (string, required)

Write a clear, concise title (2-6 words typically)
Use title case
Examples: "System Alert", "Team Update", "Training Session"

subtitle (string, optional)

Provide a secondary line directly below the title
Use it for account names, opportunities, systems, or other context
Examples: "ZenBank - Digital Channels Renewal (P1)", "Web cluster / US-East"

summary (string, optional)

Provide 1-2 sentences of descriptive text
Keep it under 100 characters when possible
Be specific and actionable
Basic markdown is supported for emphasis and lists; avoid large headings and long code blocks
Examples: "High CPU usage detected on web servers. Investigation in progress."

status (string, optional)

Provide short bottom status text shown below the summary
Examples: "Last interaction raised budget concern", "Mitigation in progress", "Review due this week"

statusPriority (string, optional)

Controls the color of the status text
Use one of: "alert", "warning", "medium", "success", "neutral"
alert: Critical or blocked
warning: At risk, caution, or concern
medium: Neutral/default state
success: Positive, resolved, or on track
neutral: Neutral/default state

**Optional Fields**

timestamp (string, optional)

Use human-readable relative time
Examples: "5 min ago", "2 hours ago", "Yesterday", "Last week"
Can also be specific dates like "March 15" or "Today at 3:PM"

badgeText: Short label for categorization (e.g., "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW", "INFO", "ERROR", "WARNING", "CRITICAL")

link (object, optional)

text: Action-oriented button text (1-3 words)

Examples: "Details", "Read More", "View", "Access", "Download"

action: Identifier for what the link does (for developers)

Use snake_case format
Examples: "view_details", "open_document", "download_file"

additionalLink (object, optional)

IMPORTANT: Only use additionalLink when link is also present. additionalLink cannot be used alone.

text: Secondary action text (1-3 words)

Examples: "Dismiss", "Later", "Learn More", "Skip"

action: Identifier for the secondary action (for developers)

Use snake_case format
Examples: "dismiss_notification", "remind_later", "skip_action"

variant (string, optional)

Use one of: "error", "warning", "info", "success", "neutral", or null
error: For critical issues, failures, alerts
warning: For cautions, upcoming issues, maintenance
info: For updates, announcements, general information
success: For positive, completed, or healthy states
neutral/null/omitted: For neutral notifications
    </instructions>
